So from the 180 degree

261
00:14:37,390 --> 00:14:39,870
spot down to zero. This

262
00:14:44,630 --> 00:14:50,210
slide demonstrates
abduction, so abduction,

263
00:14:50,210 --> 00:14:54,050
as if something is
being taken away, and

264
00:14:54,050 --> 00:14:56,510
it refers to the
movement of the shoulder

265
00:14:56,510 --> 00:15:01,890
from the arm hanging at
the side, being raised

266
00:15:01,890 --> 00:15:04,590
out to the side to
90 degrees, and then

267
00:15:04,590 --> 00:15:07,710
all the way up to the
top at 180 degrees.

268
00:15:11,470 --> 00:15:13,990
Please note the
first 15 degrees

269
00:15:13,990 --> 00:15:17,510
of abduction is
performed by the

270
00:15:17,510 --> 00:15:19,330
supraspinatus and
infraspinatus,

271
00:15:19,330 --> 00:15:21,510
after which the
deltoid takes over.

272
00:15:22,170 --> 00:15:24,790
You will have noticed
also in all of

273
00:15:24,790 --> 00:15:27,150
these slides, the
major muscles that

274
00:15:27,150 --> 00:15:30,070
contribute to this
movement are listed, and

275
00:15:30,070 --> 00:15:32,070
you should be familiar
with all of them.

276
00:15:35,380 --> 00:15:38,770
Internal rotation of
the shoulder is the

277
00:15:38,770 --> 00:15:43,570
movement in which the
thumb rotates in toward

278
00:15:43,570 --> 00:15:48,070
the body and then up
toward the scapula.

279
00:15:48,910 --> 00:15:52,450
Measuring internal
rotation is best done

280
00:15:52,450 --> 00:15:56,460
by noting the level
on the thoracic spine

281
00:15:56,460 --> 00:16:04,170
that the thumb touches
so in this case

282
00:16:04,170 --> 00:16:07,050
we would say internal
rotation of the

283
00:16:07,050 --> 00:16:11,430
shoulder on the right
to approximately t9

284
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:20,040
patient of course
is the opposite

285
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:24,200
so the thumb is
moving up away from

286
00:16:24,590 --> 00:16:28,800
the ground toward
the back of the head

287
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:33,720
And again, the best
way to document

288
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:37,140
this would be
how far down the

289
00:16:37,140 --> 00:16:39,860
cervical spine
the thumb can go.

290
00:16:46,750 --> 00:16:48,430
Strength is
tested by asking a

291
00:16:48,430 --> 00:16:50,350
patient to go
through one of the

292
00:16:50,350 --> 00:16:52,830
ranges of motion
against resistance.

293
00:16:53,290 --> 00:16:57,030
In other words, please
flex the shoulder.

294
00:16:57,370 --> 00:17:00,450
The resistance
to that flexion

295
00:17:00,450 --> 00:17:02,430
is offered by
the examiner.

296
00:17:03,170 --> 00:17:06,280
We measure the
patient's ability

297
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:08,490
to push against
that resistance

298
00:17:08,490 --> 00:17:11,210
in a motor manual
testing scale.

299
00:17:12,850 --> 00:17:15,470
This should be
performed in all ranges

300
00:17:15,470 --> 00:17:17,950
of motion when you're
examining a joint.

301
00:17:18,980 --> 00:17:21,310
The reason we use
this is so that we can

302
00:17:21,310 --> 00:17:24,530
clearly communicate with
other providers what

303
00:17:24,530 --> 00:17:27,130
kind of resistance the
patient can tolerate.

304
00:17:27,850 --> 00:17:30,170
So a zero would
mean that there's

305
00:17:30,170 --> 00:17:33,230
absolutely no muscle
movement at all, not

306
00:17:33,230 --> 00:17:35,710
even a flicker. So
a completely flaccid

307
00:17:35,710 --> 00:17:37,570
muscle, something
that you would

308
00:17:37,570 --> 00:17:41,070
only see in someone
who is paralyzed.

309
00:17:41,910 --> 00:17:44,770
And then a five means
that the patient

310
00:17:44,770 --> 00:17:49,090
can push against
strong resistance and

311
00:17:49,090 --> 00:17:51,590
that we would consider
normal. Using either

312
00:17:51,590 --> 00:17:55,390
the number or the
word is acceptable.

313
00:17:58,440 --> 00:18:01,230
Now that we have looked
at the joint, felt

314
00:18:01,230 --> 00:18:04,410
the joint, moved the
joint, and tested the

315
00:18:04,410 --> 00:18:07,110
joint strength, we can
put it through some

316
00:18:07,110 --> 00:18:10,110
specialized testing to
try to determine what

317
00:18:10,110 --> 00:18:13,270
the etiology of the
patient's complaints are.

318
00:18:14,530 --> 00:18:17,730
A crossover or
crossbody adduction test

319
00:18:17,730 --> 00:18:24,030
will test for AC
joint pain. An Apley

320
00:18:24,030 --> 00:18:30,130
Scratch Test will
check for shoulder

321
00:18:30,130 --> 00:18:36,150
rotation, and a
Painful Arc Test will

322
00:18:36,150 --> 00:18:38,410
check for a rotator
cuff tendonitis.

323
00:18:44,760 --> 00:18:46,960
Performing a Nears
Impingement sign,

324
00:18:47,420 --> 00:18:51,300
the examiner places
one arm on the

325
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:54,600
scapula and applies
a forward pressure

326
00:18:55,290 --> 00:18:57,860
while holding the
arm up with the other

327
00:18:57,860 --> 00:19:00,940
hand and applying
a backward pressure

328
00:19:01,560 --> 00:19:06,240
positive pain indicates
an impingement

329
00:19:07,520 --> 00:19:10,660
hawkins impingement
sign the

330
00:19:10,660 --> 00:19:12,940
examiner holds the
elbow with one hand

331
00:19:12,940 --> 00:19:14,960
and the forearm
with the other

332
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:19,660
Elevating the arm
at the level of

333
00:19:19,660 --> 00:19:23,420
the elbow, creating
a rotation.

334
00:19:24,740 --> 00:19:28,020
If this rotation
is painful, it

335
00:19:28,020 --> 00:19:29,980
is a positive
impingement sign.

336
00:19:35,990 --> 00:19:38,290
The test, called
the empty can test,

337
00:19:38,430 --> 00:19:40,350
checks the integrity of

338
00:19:40,350 --> 00:19:41,790
the supraspinatus tendon.

339
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:45,250
The patient is
instructed to push up

340
00:19:45,250 --> 00:19:47,470
against the resistance
of the examiner.

341
00:19:47,830 --> 00:19:51,450
and if pain is
elicited, it's an

342
00:19:51,450 --> 00:19:54,670
indication that there
is inflammation or

343
00:19:54,670 --> 00:19:56,930
injury to the
supraspinatus tendon.

344
00:19:58,790 --> 00:20:01,690
To assess rotator
cuff instability,

345
00:20:01,750 --> 00:20:04,490
the drop arm test
is very useful,

346
00:20:04,490 --> 00:20:06,710
also called the
Codman sign.

347
00:20:06,710 --> 00:20:09,330
It is performed
actively by the

348
00:20:09,330 --> 00:20:11,050
patient in a
seated position.

349
00:20:11,380 --> 00:20:14,890
The patient is asked
to abduct their arm

350
00:20:14,890 --> 00:20:18,650
to 90 degrees and
then lower it slowly.

351
00:20:18,930 --> 00:20:23,450
If the arm drops
suddenly or the patient

352
00:20:23,450 --> 00:20:27,350
is unable to lower
the arm slowly, it

353
00:20:27,350 --> 00:20:30,090
is an indication of
a rotator cuff tear.

354
00:20:32,830 --> 00:20:36,570
The apprehension test
is performed with

355
00:20:36,570 --> 00:20:39,450
the examiner pushing
anteriorly at the

356
00:20:39,450 --> 00:20:42,790
level of the shoulder
and rotating the arm

357
00:20:42,790 --> 00:20:47,370
in an external rotation
from the forearm.

358
00:20:47,670 --> 00:20:50,170
The patient becomes
apprehensive

359
00:20:50,170 --> 00:20:52,890
if they feel
that the shoulder

360
00:20:52,890 --> 00:20:55,150
is going to
dislocate anteriorly,

361
00:20:56,340 --> 00:20:59,430
hence the term
apprehension test. This

362
00:21:04,250 --> 00:21:06,710
is a slide depicting
the Jurgesson's test.

363
00:21:07,210 --> 00:21:10,070
Jurgesson test assesses

364
00:21:10,070 --> 00:21:12,510
the long head
of the bicep.

365
00:21:13,830 --> 00:21:17,210
As a provider, you
will be holding the

366
00:21:17,210 --> 00:21:22,110
patient's arm at his
side by the elbow and

367
00:21:22,110 --> 00:21:25,150
applying a resistance
to supination at the

368
00:21:25,150 --> 00:21:28,510
forearm. your instructions
to the patient

369
00:21:28,510 --> 00:21:32,230
are to raise their arm
away from their body

370
00:21:32,650 --> 00:21:36,730
in an external
rotation movement

371
00:21:36,730 --> 00:21:40,490
while trying to
supinate the arm

372
00:21:41,350 --> 00:21:45,310
a positive test again
indicates damage or

373
00:21:45,310 --> 00:21:47,870
inflammation to the
long head of the bicep

374
00:21:51,410 --> 00:21:53,830
here are just some
pearls regarding

375
00:21:53,830 --> 00:21:55,410
making a shoulder
diagnosis

376
00:21:55,970 --> 00:21:58,370
remember that a
C5 radiculopathy

377
00:21:58,370 --> 00:22:00,570
can masquerade
as shoulder pain.

378
00:22:01,870 --> 00:22:06,490
If the injury occurred
during a sport such

379
00:22:06,490 --> 00:22:08,730
as a throwing sport
or a racket sport,

380
00:22:08,750 --> 00:22:11,690
you've got to
find out at which

381
00:22:11,690 --> 00:22:14,510
phase the
injury occurred.

382
00:22:16,750 --> 00:22:19,870
If there was a
posterior dislocation,

383
00:22:19,870 --> 00:22:22,170
the arm was
usually in internal

384
00:22:22,170 --> 00:22:24,190
rotation at the
time of injury.

385
00:22:24,470 --> 00:22:27,010
And concomitantly, if
there's an anterior

386
00:22:27,010 --> 00:22:29,410
dislocation, the
arm is usually an

387
00:22:29,410 --> 00:22:31,510
external rotation at
the time of injury.

388
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:42,040
When we evaluate the
elbow, we take the

389
00:22:42,040 --> 00:22:45,240
same steps as we did
when evaluating the

390
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:48,040
shoulder. So first,
we're going to inspect

391
00:22:48,040 --> 00:22:50,960
the elbow, looking
for lumps, bumps scars

392
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:54,920
bruises any sign of
inflammation or injury

393
00:22:57,700 --> 00:23:01,020
when we palpate we
should be able to

394
00:23:01,020 --> 00:23:04,200
feel both epicondyles
and the olecranon

395
00:23:04,200 --> 00:23:09,300
process the ulnar nerve
is very superficial

396
00:23:09,300 --> 00:23:12,970
in the ulnar groove
and can be very tender

397
00:23:12,970 --> 00:23:15,160
so be careful when
you're examining it

398
00:23:21,740 --> 00:23:24,020
some common sites
of pain in the elbow

399
00:23:24,020 --> 00:23:28,420
include the medial
epicondyle where you

400
00:23:28,420 --> 00:23:31,660
will get a medial
epicondylitis same with

401
00:23:31,660 --> 00:23:36,880
the lateral epicondyle
as well as compression

402
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:40,360
or irritation of
the ulnar nerve as

403
00:23:40,360 --> 00:23:42,340
it courses through
the ulnar groove like

404
00:23:49,050 --> 00:23:50,590
the shoulder with
its unlimited

405
00:23:50,590 --> 00:23:52,190
potential for movement

406
00:23:52,650 --> 00:23:56,130
and subsequent
instability the elbow

407
00:23:56,130 --> 00:23:58,470
movement is much
more limited but that

408
00:23:58,470 --> 00:24:00,790
makes the joint also
much more stable.

409
00:24:01,430 --> 00:24:06,050
The elbow can simply
bend and extend,

410
00:24:06,590 --> 00:24:08,710
pronate and supinate.

411
00:24:09,410 --> 00:24:11,290
Please note the
muscles that are

412
00:24:11,290 --> 00:24:13,510
involved with each
of those movements.

413
00:24:15,150 --> 00:24:17,350
Pronation involves
turning the

414
00:24:17,350 --> 00:24:18,830
palm down toward
the ground.

415
00:24:19,130 --> 00:24:21,430
Supination involves
turning the palm

416
00:24:21,430 --> 00:24:23,190
up as if you're
going to try to

417
00:24:23,190 --> 00:24:26,430
carry some soup
with your supination

418
00:24:26,760 --> 00:24:29,770
and then bending
your elbows flexion

419
00:24:29,770 --> 00:24:31,530
and straightening
it is extension

420
00:24:37,630 --> 00:24:40,990
again the motor
manual testing is used

421
00:24:40,990 --> 00:24:44,900
to assess strength
in this case flexion

422
00:24:46,450 --> 00:24:48,070
and extension so

423
00:24:56,410 --> 00:25:00,330
now that we have
inspected and palpated

424
00:25:00,390 --> 00:25:04,050
moved and assessed
the strength of our

425
00:25:04,050 --> 00:25:06,170
elbow, we can go
into special testing.

426
00:25:06,730 --> 00:25:09,690
The first special
test is the Tunnels.

427
00:25:09,830 --> 00:25:12,870
The Tunnels is a
test where you tap

428
00:25:12,870 --> 00:25:15,490
over a nerve, looking
for nerve irritation.

429
00:25:15,550 --> 00:25:20,510
It is not only
done at the elbow,

430
00:25:20,510 --> 00:25:22,610
it's also done at
the wrist if you're

431
00:25:22,610 --> 00:25:25,450
looking for median
nerve irritation as

432
00:25:25,450 --> 00:25:28,110
seen in carpal tunnel
or or in the ankle

433
00:25:28,110 --> 00:25:29,690
if you're looking
for tarsal tunnel.

434
00:25:31,660 --> 00:25:34,710
We also can do
a COSINS test to

435
00:25:34,710 --> 00:25:36,840
assess for lateral
epicondylitis,

436
00:25:36,930 --> 00:25:39,030
also known as
tennis elbow.

437
00:25:40,040 --> 00:25:44,030
To perform a COSINS
test, the patient is

438
00:25:44,030 --> 00:25:46,310
asked to extend their
wrist against strong

439
00:25:46,310 --> 00:25:49,410
resistance provided
by the examiner.

440
00:25:50,220 --> 00:25:52,110
If there is pain
on the lateral

441
00:25:52,110 --> 00:25:54,770
epicondyle,
the patient may

442
00:25:54,770 --> 00:25:57,470
indeed have
lateral epicondyl

443
00:25:58,090 --> 00:26:02,150
similarly on the
medial aspect you can

444
00:26:02,150 --> 00:26:05,070
assess for medial
epicondylitis also known

445
00:26:05,070 --> 00:26:08,230
as golfer's elbow by
asking a patient to

446
00:26:08,230 --> 00:26:11,710
flex the wrist
against resistance and

447
00:26:11,710 --> 00:26:14,170
assessing for pain at
the medial epicondyle

448
00:26:20,110 --> 00:26:22,750
so just a few words
about making a diagnosis

449
00:26:22,750 --> 00:26:27,110
at the elbow the
extensors and supinators

450
00:26:27,110 --> 00:26:29,310
of the wrist attach
at the lateral

451
00:26:29,310 --> 00:26:33,090
epicondyle whereas the
flexors and pronators

452
00:26:33,090 --> 00:26:36,690
attach at the
medial epicondyle so

453
00:26:36,690 --> 00:26:39,690
inflammation at one
or the other of those

454
00:26:39,690 --> 00:26:42,270
locations gives you
an indication of what

455
00:26:42,270 --> 00:26:45,890
movements might be
painful and by all means

456
00:26:45,890 --> 00:26:49,050
don't miss a tendon
rupture dislocation

457
00:26:49,510 --> 00:26:51,050
or fracture here

458
00:26:57,370 --> 00:27:01,190
is a list of some of
the diagnoses you will

459
00:27:01,190 --> 00:27:03,650
come across when
examining the shoulder

460
00:27:03,650 --> 00:27:05,810
The more common ones, of

461
00:27:05,810 --> 00:27:08,270
course, rotator
cuff pathology,

462
00:27:09,370 --> 00:27:11,950
glenohumeral
head instability,

463
00:27:13,370 --> 00:27:16,130
bicep tears and
tendinopathies,

464
00:27:21,450 --> 00:27:22,410
as well as scapular

465
00:27:22,410 --> 00:27:23,790
pathology and
dysfunction.

466
00:27:24,950 --> 00:27:28,490
Less common
diagnoses you'll

467
00:27:28,490 --> 00:27:31,250
see are other
muscle tears,

468
00:27:31,730 --> 00:27:34,610
adhesive capsulitis,
also known as frozen

469
00:27:34,610 --> 00:27:38,890
shoulder, nerve
entrapments, and fractures.

470
00:27:49,220 --> 00:27:52,060
Regarding the elbow, if

471
00:27:52,240 --> 00:27:53,760
the pain is anteriorly,

472
00:27:54,540 --> 00:27:57,640
look for bicep
tendinopathies,

473
00:27:58,360 --> 00:27:59,740
pronative syndrome,

474
00:28:00,100 --> 00:28:01,920
gout, rheumatoid
arthritis.

475
00:28:02,660 --> 00:28:04,460
If the pain is lateral,

476
00:28:04,780 --> 00:28:08,540
look for lateral
epicondylitis or

477
00:28:08,540 --> 00:28:12,120
osteochondral defect or
radial tunnel syndrome.

478
00:28:12,580 --> 00:28:17,180
If it's medial,
consider cubital

479
00:28:17,180 --> 00:28:20,100
tunnel syndrome,
medial epicondylitis,

480
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:22,700
ulnar collateral
ligament injury.

481
00:28:23,100 --> 00:28:26,200
And if it's
posterior, consider

482
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:28,760
olecranon stress
fracture or brusitis,

483
00:28:29,200 --> 00:28:30,800
osteoarthritis,

484
00:28:31,080 --> 00:28:33,260
posterior impingement, or

485
00:28:33,260 --> 00:28:34,560
tricep tendinopathy. And

486
00:28:39,730 --> 00:28:41,960
if you have any
questions regarding

487
